    <p class="font-bold mt-2">
      Reflecting the public will in policy: building a platform for large-scale online deliberation
    </p>
  </hgroup>
  <img
    src="/idobata/home__3project__idobata.webp"
    width="576"
    height="324"
    alt="Illustration of Idobata"
    class="w-full"
  />
  <p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
    Idobata is a project to build a large-scale deliberation platform so that citizens in Japan, too, can take part in policymaking, drawing on pioneering examples from Taiwan such as "JOIN" and "vTaiwan".
  </p>
  <p class="max-w-xl mt-4">
    Specifically, by using AI at each of the following three steps, it aims to go beyond simple majority voting, organize the issues under discussion from many angles, and support constructive consensus-building and policymaking:
  </p>
  <ol class="max-w-xl mt-4 list-decimal pl-8">
    <li>Identifying the issues to discuss</li>
    <li>Considering and discussing solutions</li>
    <li>Evaluating solutions and building consensus</li>
  </ol>
  <section>
    <h3 class="text-2xl mt-10">Next steps</h3>
    <p class="mt-4">
      We intend to make tools that support discussion and consensus-building widely available to local governments and political parties, with each local government or party that wants to run a pilot deciding how to adopt and operate them.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      We are currently finalizing the specifications, and will publish details once the conditions for adoption are in place.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="flex gap-4 mt-20">
